  154:  Wed 20 Jan 1993  15:11:05 :
Colin at NMS reported that fwd refs to label equ's to *-(rel 0) give rel 0
as the result.  Verified and fixed.
[BUILD]   AS  : 1134 

  155:  Wed 24 Feb 1993  16:29:27 :
Motorola-style radix suffered from change of precedence of *.  Disallowed
as multiply when in Motorola style.

[BUILD]   AS  : 1144 

  156:  Thu 04 Mar 1993  15:23:06 :
Subtraction code in the Assembler checked if two args were relative, but
failed to ensure they were relative to the same base address.  Fixed and
tested on T.ASM.  Bug pointed out by Tony at Hybrid after adding Segment
caused failures in data tables produced from cross-segment subtractions.

[BUILD]   AS  : 1152 

  157:  Sat 20 Mar 1993  13:17:00 :
Implemented transient labels - if definition begins with '@' then scope
lasts only until next normal label definition.  String symbols and macro
calls by themseleves do not cause end of scope.

[BUILD]   AS  : 1173 

  158:  Sat 20 Mar 1993  15:31:32 :
Added Pseudo-op for getting named file size into a label FILESIZE - takes
filename in double-quotes as its argument.

  159:  Sat 20 Mar 1993  15:32:15 :
Added facility for giving an ellipsis (...) at the end of a macro's formal
parameter list.  If given, strings passed in the normal way after any
other formal paramters are fed into _arg1.._argn.  _arg0 holds the number
of parameters passed, from 1 upward.  The _argX parameters follow exactly
the same scope rules as ther normal parameters.

  160:  Sat 20 Mar 1993  15:35:25 :
Added capability for dereferencing numeric labels, if preceded by an &, eg
label&num, where num is a numeric label, will give label5 if num==5.  If
the numeric label's name is coming from a string symbol, give an extra &
to get the extra dereferencing.  Example: string symbol 'str'=='num', and
numeric symbol num==5.  label&str gives 'labelnum' and label&&str gives
'label5'.  If 'label' itself is a string symbol, it will use up the first &
during its own dereferencing, so add an extra & in that case.


[BUILD]   AS  : 1201 

  161:  Tue 23 Mar 1993  00:13:09 :
Changed Source-grabbing code to cache in (currently) 16K units.  On an
uncached hard drive, this improved performance on Ade's test file from
70 ticks to 55, where the reference assembler (6.01) was 52 ticks.  The
lowest level dos file IO routines are used, so expect improvements in
all situations showing slowdown.

